Index: code/data/changelog.dm
===================================================================
--- code/data/changelog.dm	(revision 249)
+++ code/data/changelog.dm	(working copy)
@@ -3,6 +3,18 @@
 <P>This version is a fork of Rick's currently running server,
 and is a testbed of proposed fixes, changes, and features.</p>
 <HR>
+<P><B>Persh's Notes:</b><BR>
+<ul>
+<li>Engineers are required if you want to have power beyond the first 10 minutes. Serious business.</li>
+<li>By default the station requires approximately 215,000 watts of power, be sure to set the batteries to the correct inputs and outputs.</li>
+<li>The AI also requires an additional 25,00 watts on top of whatever the station load shows, so account for that unless you want the AI's battery to slowly die.</li>
+<li>Adding CO2 to the hot loop once it is being circulated is a bad idea. CO2 cools it down. Try adding it to the cold loop for a better effect</li>
+<li>A good way to start the engine is to simply set both loops to 100% until the engine is at full blast (Should be getting 200,000 worth at this time) and then slowly tamper the cold loop down</li>
+<li>The O2 indicators on the walls can be cut. Should probably do this if you don't want the AI to be notified of your explosive schemes</li>
+<li>EVA storage has a motion camera. Stay around too long and the AI is gonna know. Disable that bitch</li>
+<li>MVirus mode :]</li>
+</ul>
+</p
 
 <P><B>Modified Tuesday, June 24th 2008 (Revision 233):</b><BR>
